    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d483">

                <pb facs="0668" n="578" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg578"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.85/966</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the British Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Geddes</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-26"><hi rendition="#italic">December 26,
                        1919</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: Referring to your note of December
                    19, 1919, in regard to former German vessels which the British Government
                    desires to have delivered to the British authorities, I have the honor to inform
                    you that I am now advised by the competent authorities of this Government that
                    the steamships <hi rendition="#italic">Graf Waldersee, Zeppelin, Pretoria, Cap
                        Finisterre, Mobile, Prinz Friederich Wilhelm</hi>, and <pb facs="0669"
                        n="579" xml:id="pg579"/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Kaiserin Augusta Victoria</hi>, now in the harbor of New
                    York, will be delivered to the representative of your Government as soon as the
                    proper person is designated to receive them.<anchor n="69" xml:id="d483-f1"
                    /></p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Frank L. Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d483-f1" n="69" xml:id="d483-f1-content">
                <p>For the British claim arising out of the detention of these vessels and of the
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Imperator</hi>, See <ref target="#pg648">p.
                        648</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
